      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think that this should be restricted to AndroidLibraryDependency I think it should just use Dependency. I know that the previous code did restrict it to AndroidLibraryDependency so switching to Dependency would be a functional change (and separated out into its own change) but I think that at the moment we will not track dependencies correctly. e.g. say we have something like this:\n\njava_sdk_library {\n   name: \"runtime-library\",\n}\n\njava_library {\n   name: \"static-runtime-helper\",\n   libs: [\"runtime-library\"],\n}\n\nandroid_app {\n   name: \"app\",\n   static_libs: [\n      \"static-runtime-helper\",\n   ],\n}\n\nThen \"app\" should have \"runtime-library\" added to its \u003cuses-library\u003e but I don\u0027t think it will.\n\nI tested it and it doesn\u0027t seem to work as it should so I raised http://b/163037089 to fix it and assigned it to you.",
